# Unit and integration tests

- Prefer parametrized tests to reduce duplication and improve coverage.
- Follow the same code style and conventions as the rest of the project.
- Do not mock database sessions.
- Mirror production logic expectations in tests (same rules, no shortcuts).
- Use polyfactory for test data where it fits.
- Keep factories under the `all_factories` folder when present.
- Use `factory_creators`, `factory_getters`, and `factory_updaters` for creating, fetching, and updating test data; add these helpers when missing.
- Prefer comparing full objects over field-by-field assertions unless a focused assertion is required.
- Do not add imports inside functions.
- Remove or use variables; avoid dead assignments.
- When asserting API error responses, assert status and response body/detail, not only status code.
